<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates higher in quiet market.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates higher in quiet market.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were higher on Tuesday in line with the rising domestic interest rates, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Banks were raising their offers for pesos after some decided to borrow from the swap market to lend to the central bank,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>Banks were borrowing pesos in the PHIBOR market to invest them in the Central Bank's overnight borrowing facility which was offering 32 percent interest yield.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  JULY 15		 JULY 14</p>
<p>    1 W		31 13/16		31  3/16</p>
<p>    2 W		29  3/4		 29  1/16</p>
<p>    1 M		26 15/16		25  9/16</p>
<p>    2 M		22 11/16		21  1/2</p>
<p>    3 M		20  1/8		 18  3/8</p>
<p>    6 M		17  1/4		 16  3/16</p>
<p>    12M		16  9/16		15  5/8</p>
<p>    VAL		16-Jul		  15-Jul</p>
<p>-- Lilian Karunungan (63 2) 841-8937</p>
